meta {
  name: Prometheus Metrics
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/metrics
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Prometheus scrape endpoint — returns all metrics in the standard text
  exposition format. No authentication required (Prometheus scrapes it
  from inside the Docker network).

  Key metric families:

  Standard HTTP:
  - `llm_gateway_requests_total`          — request count by method, path, status
  - `llm_gateway_request_duration_seconds` — latency histogram (p50/p95/p99)
  - `llm_gateway_request_size_bytes`       — request body size histogram
  - `llm_gateway_response_size_bytes`      — response body size histogram

  RAG-specific:
  - `llm_gateway_rag_cost_usd_total`       — cumulative cost by team + operation
  - `llm_gateway_budget_utilisation`       — daily budget fraction by team (0–1)
  - `llm_gateway_circuit_breaker_state`    — CB state gauge (0=CLOSED, 1=OPEN, 2=HALF_OPEN) by provider + model
  - `llm_gateway_fallback_total`           — fallback event count by from_model + to_model + reason

  These metrics power all three Grafana dashboards:
  - http://localhost:3000/d/rag-cost-attribution
  - http://localhost:3000/d/operations
  - http://localhost:3000/d/teams-budget
}
